= Distributed system — Simple =

A '''distributed system''' uses several computers that communicate over a network and work together as one larger service or computation.

Examples include cloud services, distributed databases, and large web systems.

Distributed systems are difficult because computers can fail separately and messages can be delayed or lost.

There is also no perfect shared clock telling every machine exactly what happened first.

A computer network connects machines.

A distributed system uses that network to coordinate computation and state.

